    method
        • both explanantia, present and alternative, can be characterized as sharing the same form:
          multiverse ensemble hypothesis of fine tuning + extra premise(s)
            : re `present`     see `^^multiverse ensemble \+.design$`i             @ text_boneyard.brec
            : re `alternative` see `^^multiverse ensemble \+.physical necessity$`i @ text_boneyard.brec
            - moreover the extra premise(s) in each case can be characterized as borrowed
              from one of the other two hypotheses of fine tuning
                : re `other two hypotheses of fine tuning` see `^*•.+physical necessity$` @
                  01.tale-of-logic_form/._/40.a_search_for_explanations.notes.brec : present case
                : re `other two hypotheses of fine tuning` see `^*•.+design$` @
                  01.tale-of-logic_form/._/40.a_search_for_explanations.notes.brec : alternative
                    : re `design` viz. `a version of.+${same}.+based wholly on natural premises`
                      @ `^^authorial priority$`i @ text.notes.brec :
                      not one of the (typical) theistic versions, that is
            + order the text by these characteristics, deferring presentation of the alternative
              explanans pending consideration|vetting of the design hypothesis
                - treating both multiverse-ensemble and design hypotheses equitably apropos
                  and on account of their symmetric shortcomings and prospects for repair
                    / each being reparable, that is, by extra premise(s) taken|borrowed from the other
                / this should, finally, suffice to start drafting
                + juxtapose complete with their premises all explantia for the reader to compare
                    - so much for the aetiology: no need to argue here for my own explanans
        • the extra premise needed by the multiverse ensemble hypothesis in order to explain not only
          fine tuning, but also the presence of the safehold, is hard to judge and must be looked into
            : ad `to judge` : rival explanantia are to be judged by scrutiny of the extra premises
              that each needs in order to cover also the added|extra explanandum of safeholding
            - good for the purpose would be a property break-out and comparison table,
              comparing for each property:
                    (a) the range of its values necessary for habitability
                    (b) the range sufficient for safeholding
                - then ask, re a random structure of reality that happens to deliver (a) habitability:
                  how likely that it also happen to deliver (b) safeholding?
                - this gives a measure by which to judge whether the degree of coupling is as tight
                  as premised, viz. whether we could hardly have (a) without also having (b)
            ? property values for the habitability column from the fine-tuning and multiverse literature
                : see https://scholar.google.ca/scholar_labs/search/session/11918491117785400852 :
                 ‘Where in the literature on cosmological fine tuning or multiverse do scholars address
                  how the habitability of the universe (whether for life, or for observers like us)
                  relates to the speed limit of *c* that it imposes on causation?’ (2026-6-3)
                    : see https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=5376662 :
                      Besemer, David A.  2025.  ‘Universal time formula cosmology: emergent time
                      and the unification of fundamental physics.’  August 2, 2025 draft.
                          His multiverse model tightly couples habitability to the imposition
                      of a safehold-consistent speed limit.  ‘Life-supporting constraints
                      for complex chemistry and biology: 0.5 ≲ R ≲ 2 …  This narrow range
                      [for the speed of light] ensures:
                          • Stable atomic structure
                          • Liquid water phase
                          • Complex molecular chemistry
                          • Sufficient evolutionary time’  p. 59
                      These claims he makes, but gives no argument for.
                    - precise values are still speculative
                        / together with the nature of the multiverse, indeed with its very presence
                if( a value range is imprecise )
                    / as I expect the more reliable ones will be
                    + so express it by a descriptor
